  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Dell Federal Systems L P recorded $1.2B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Dell Federal Systems L P won 421 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.8M. Dell Federal Systems L P's obligations are down 10.3% year over year. Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $512M, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $246M and Department of Health and Human Services at $138M. Software Publishers is the dominant market by NAICS with $952M in obligations, far ahead of the next entry in that category at $125M. Historical obligations show multi-year scale: FY21 $1.6B, FY22 $1.7B, FY23 $1.4B, FY24 $1.5B, FY25 $1.3B, and FY26 $1.2B. The Department of Defense obligated $131M and Department of Commerce obligated $56.4M in the current fiscal year. The dataset covers contract obligations except where tables list total contract values for largest awards and expiring contracts. This summary focuses on FY2026 to date, which is a partial fiscal-year total.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Dell Federal Systems L P's biggest government customers?",
        "body": "Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $512M in FY2026 to date. Department of Homeland Security and Department of Health and Human Services follow with $246M and $138M respectively. Department of Defense obligated $131M, and Department of Commerce obligated $56.4M, making those agencies significant buyers as well."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and contract types drive Dell Federal Systems L P's federal work?",
        "body": "Software Publishers is the top market by far with $952M in obligations, followed by a second Software Publishers entry at $125M and Other Computer Related Services at $59.8M. Electronic Computer Manufacturing and Computer Storage Device Manufacturing contributed $52.7M and $4.6M respectively, indicating technology and software dominate the company’s federal portfolio."
      }
    ]
  },
